    "description": "A finite sequence of vectors, written as a parenthesised comma-separated list: (a, b, c). Semantically a function Fin n → T, not a product type. Mathlib counterpart: the vector notation in Mathlib/Data/Fin/VecNotation.lean (`syntax \"![\" term,* \"]\"`, expanding to `vecCons`/`vecEmpty` over `Fin n → α`). This is a notation facility rather than a constant, so the macro takes the facility's file name. Placed in BasicOperators for now — it is notation crossing several theories; to be split out later.",
